{"id":"naep__nqt_9826","bank":"naep","year":2009,"level":"High school","grade":12,"unit":"Grade 12","batch":"naep_1_12_2009_number_operations","number":305,"area":"Number Properties and Operations","topic":{"id":"naep_1_12_2009_number_operations","label":"2009 Grade 12, Number Properties and Operations"},"domain":["domain:number-algebra"],"skill":[],"responseType":"choice","question":"The manager of a company has to order new engines for its delivery trucks after the trucks have been driven 150,000 miles. One of the delivery trucks currently has 119,866 miles on it. This truck has the same delivery route each week and is driven an average of 40,000 miles each year. At this rate, the manager should expect this truck to reach 150,000 miles in approximately how many months?","questionType":"text","choices":{"A":"Less than 4 months","B":"Between 4 and 6 months","C":"Between 6 and 8 months","D":"Between 8 and 10 months","E":"More than 10 months"},"choiceOrder":["A","B","C","D","E"],"choicesType":"text","answer":"D","acceptedResponses":["D"],"rejectedAnswers":[],"unorderedAnswers":false,"solution":"The truck will reach \\(150{,}000\\) miles in about nine months. It has \\(150{,}000-119{,}866=30{,}134\\) miles to go, a little over three quarters of its \\(40{,}000\\)-mile annual distance. Three quarters of \\(12\\) months is nine months.","solutionMethods":[{"id":"worked","label":"Work through the question","explanation":"The truck will reach \\(150{,}000\\) miles in about nine months. It has \\(150{,}000-119{,}866=30{,}134\\) miles to go, a little over three quarters of its \\(40{,}000\\)-mile annual distance. Three quarters of \\(12\\) months is nine months.","provenance":{"source":"AI-authored worked explanation for Ailleo Math Practice","attribution":"Ailleo Math Practice","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","licenseURL":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/","reviewStatus":"Checked against the official key during intake. No teacher review.","sourceRef":"naep/naep__nqt_9826#worked"}}],"sourceInfo":{"kind":"question","label":"2009 NAEP mathematics, grade 12, item M180801","attribution":"SOURCE: U.S. Department of Education, Institute of Education Sciences, National Center for Education Statistics, National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP), 2009 Mathematics Assessment.","license":"U.S. public domain per NAEP Questions Tool copyright policy","licenseURL":"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/nqt/#copyrightpolicy","sourceURL":"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/nqt/api/queryresults/GetItem?tableID=9826","revision":"2009-12M7 #5 M180801","position":{"batch":"naep_1_12_2009_number_operations","year":2009,"number":64},"adaptation":"Publisher prompt and choices converted from HTML to plain text.","officialKeyURL":"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/nqt/api/queryresults/GetItemScoreGuide?tableID=9826"},"schemaVersion":"3.0","sourceRef":"naep/naep__nqt_9826","figureSources":{},"sourceURL":"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/nqt/api/queryresults/GetItem?tableID=9826","solutionSource":"AI-authored worked explanation for Ailleo Math Practice","solutionSourceURL":"","editorialNote":"","translationStatus":"","solutionAvailability":"present","solutionOmittedReason":"","solutionStatus":"","sourceId":"naep","sourceQuestionId":"naep__nqt_9826","sourceNumber":64,"assessedNodeIds":[]}
